    "q-5193": {
      "dom_id": "step-q5193",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find the center and radius of the circle whose equation is ${x}^{2}-4x+{y}^{2}-20y+88=0.$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the center and radius of the circle, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4x+{y}^{2}-20y+88 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4x)+({y}^{2}-20y) & =-88 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 10y+{10}^{2}) & =-88+{2}^{2}+{10}^{2} \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 2x+{2}^{2})+({y}^{2}-2\\cdot 10y+{10}^{2}) & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can factor the perfect squares and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & ={4}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(2,10)$ and its radius is $4.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
